#: ../../../command/string.rst:415
msgid "``%w``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:416
msgid "The day of the current week. 0 is Sunday. (0-6)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:418
msgid "``%a``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:421
msgid "Abbreviated weekday name (e.g. Fri)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:423
msgid "``%A``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:426
msgid "Full weekday name (e.g. Friday)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:428
msgid "``%y``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:429
msgid "The last two digits of the current year (00-99)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:431
msgid "``%Y``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:432
msgid "The current year."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:434
msgid "``%z``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:437
msgid ""
"The offset of the time zone from UTC, in hours and minutes, with format "
"``+hhmm`` or ``-hhmm``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:440
msgid "``%Z``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:443
msgid "The time zone name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:445
msgid ""
"Unknown format specifiers will be ignored and copied to the output as-is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:448
msgid "If no explicit ``<format_string>`` is given, it will default to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:450
msgid "``%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S`` for local time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:451
msgid "``%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`` for UTC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:453
msgid ""
"If the ``SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`` environment variable is set, its value will be "
"used instead of the current time. See https://reproducible-builds.org/specs/"
"source-date-epoch/ for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:464
msgid ""
"Create a universally unique identifier (aka GUID) as per RFC4122 based on "
"the hash of the combined values of ``<namespace>`` (which itself has to be a "
"valid UUID) and ``<name>``. The hash algorithm can be either ``MD5`` "
"(Version 3 UUID) or ``SHA1`` (Version 5 UUID). A UUID has the format "
"``xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx`` where each ``x`` represents a lower "
"case hexadecimal character. Where required, an uppercase representation can "
"be requested with the optional ``UPPER`` flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:477
msgid "JSON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:481
msgid "Functionality for querying a JSON string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:484
msgid ""
"In each of the following JSON-related subcommands, if the optional "
"``ERROR_VARIABLE`` argument is given, errors will be reported in ``<error-"
"variable>`` and the ``<out-var>`` will be set to ``<member|index>-[<member|"
"index>...]-NOTFOUND`` with the path elements up to the point where the error "
"occurred, or just ``NOTFOUND`` if there is no relevant path.  If an error "
"occurs but the ``ERROR_VARIABLE`` option is not present, a fatal error "
"message is generated.  If no error occurs, the ``<error-variable>`` will be "
"set to ``NOTFOUND``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:493
msgid ""
"In the following subcommands, the ``<json-string>`` argument should be "
"written as a :ref:`Quoted Argument` to ensure the entire JSON string is "
"passed as a single argument even if it contains semicolons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:502
msgid ""
"Get an element from ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the list of "
"``<member|index>`` arguments. Array and object elements will be returned as "
"a JSON string. Boolean elements will be returned as ``ON`` or ``OFF``. Null "
"elements will be returned as an empty string. Number and string types will "
"be returned as strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:516
msgid ""
"Get an element from ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the list of "
"``<member|index>`` arguments. Similar to :cref:`GET <JSON-GET_>`, but does "
"not convert number, string, boolean, or null elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:526
msgid ""
"Get the type of an element in ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the "
"list of ``<member|index>`` arguments. The ``<out-var>`` will be set to one "
"of ``NULL``, ``NUMBER``, ``STRING``, ``BOOLEAN``, ``ARRAY``, or ``OBJECT``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:537
msgid ""
"Get the name of the ``<index>``-th member in ``<json-string>`` at the "
"location given by the list of ``<member|index>`` arguments. Requires an "
"element of object type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:546
msgid ""
"Get the length of an element in ``<json-string>`` at the location given by "
"the list of ``<member|index>`` arguments. Requires an element of array or "
"object type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:557
msgid ""
"Split the array in ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the list of "
"``<member|index>`` arguments into a :ref:`semicolon-separated list <CMake "
"Language Lists>`, one entry per array element.  Requires an element of array "
"type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:562
msgid ""
"This enables iterating an array with a single parse of ``<json-string>``, "
"instead of re-parsing the whole string for each element:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:565
msgid ""
"string(JSON elements ARRAY_SPLIT \"${json}\")\n"
"foreach(element IN LISTS elements)\n"
"  string(JSON value GET \"${element}\" some_member)\n"
"endforeach()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:572
msgid ""
"Each entry is the corresponding element re-serialized as compact JSON.  It "
"is *semantically* equal to the source element (as compared by :cref:`EQUAL "
"<JSON-EQUAL_>`), but not necessarily byte-for-byte identical: insignificant "
"whitespace is removed and object members may be reordered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:577
msgid ""
"The result is a regular CMake list and should be consumed with list-aware "
"constructs such as :command:`foreach(IN LISTS) <foreach>` or the :command:"
"`list` command.  Elements may contain characters that are encoded to keep "
"the list well-formed, so operating on the raw ``<out-var>`` value with plain "
"string operations may expose that internal encoding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:588
msgid ""
"Remove an element from ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the list "
"of ``<member|index>`` arguments. The JSON string without the removed element "
"will be stored in ``<out-var>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:597
msgid ""
"Set an element in ``<json-string>`` at the location given by the list of "
"``<member|index>`` arguments to ``<value>``. The contents of ``<value>`` "
"should be valid JSON. If ``<json-string>`` is an array, ``<value>`` can be "
"appended to the end of the array by using a number greater or equal to the "
"array length as the ``<member|index>`` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:609
msgid ""
"Compare the two JSON objects given by ``<json-string1>`` and ``<json-"
"string2>`` for equality.  The contents of ``<json-string1>`` and ``<json-"
"string2>`` should be valid JSON.  The ``<out-var>`` will be set to a true "
"value if the JSON objects are considered equal, or a false value otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:622
msgid ""
"Compare two JSON values using *partial* equality.  The first argument "
"(``<json-pattern>``) is treated as a pattern to match against the second "
"argument (``<json-actual>``), which is treated as the complete JSON value. "
"The contents of ``<json-pattern>`` and ``<json-actual>`` must be valid JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:627
msgid ""
"The ``<out-var>`` will be set to a true value if ``<json-pattern>`` is "
"contained within ``<json-actual>`` according to the rules below, or a false "
"value otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:631
msgid ""
"Partial equality is not symmetric.  In general, ``PARTIAL_EQUAL(A, B)`` and "
"``PARTIAL_EQUAL(B, A)`` may produce different results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:635
msgid "Matching rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:637
msgid "**Scalars** (null, number, string, boolean) must match exactly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:638
msgid ""
"**Objects** match if every member in ``<json-pattern>`` exists in ``<json-"
"actual>`` and the corresponding values also match recursively. Extra members "
"in ``<json-actual>`` are ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:641
msgid ""
"**Arrays** match if every element in ``<json-pattern>`` matches a distinct "
"element in ``<json-actual>`` recursively. Once an element in ``<json-"
"actual>`` successfully matches an element in ``<json-pattern>``, it is "
"consumed and cannot be reused to match any subsequent elements. Array "
"element order is not significant.  Extra elements in ``<json-actual>`` are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:648
msgid ""
"Type differences do not match (for example, an object does not match an "
"array, and a string does not match a number)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../command/string.rst:658
msgid ""
"Turn a raw string into a JSON string surrounded by quotes. Special "
"characters will be properly escaped inside the JSON string."
msgstr ""
